FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode owns the most code that is still here. Douglas Christopher Wilson is second.

I ran `git blame` on every line at HEAD across the 18 tracked files, excluding lockfiles and images. I used `-w -M -C`, which ignores whitespace and follows moved and copied lines.

The latest commit, `62628c0` ("reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes"), touched about 1,000 lines and credits them to "Fiona Formatter". I excluded it with `--ignore-rev` so those lines go back to whoever wrote the logic. The raw numbers are in the last paragraph.

| Author | Lines | Share |
|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 810 | 40.6% |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 629 | 31.5% |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | 4.8% |
| Jon Church | 72 | 3.6% |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | 3.4% |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | 2.6% |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 | 2.2% |
| Other 39 authors | 226 | 11.3% |

The total is 1,995 lines from 46 authors.

- **Two people own about 72% of the surviving lines.** The next author is under 5%.
- **Commit counts rank the top two the other way round.** Douglas has 143 commits and Troy has 122. Troy's code lasted longer. A rewrite could change that, since most of Troy's lines are probably in `test/test.js` and similar test files.
- **The 46 authors overlap with 12 listed in the top table.** The rest each own only a handful of lines.
- **With the reformat commit counted, "Fiona Formatter" is third.** It gets 291 lines (about 14.6%), and Troy and Douglas drop to 715 and 454 lines. That figure reflects the style change, not who wrote the code.

I did not split ownership by file. `lib/index.js` is the core code and may have a different top owner than the repo overall. I can run that next if you want it.
